  "Interpretation": [
    "The D median is already elevated before the opening cue. Complete-panel construction cannot explain that pre-existing gap.",
    "D2/D3 return close to their own pre-open median after the closing cue. D1 has a disclosed late close of unknown duration, so its late window is not claimed as a fully controlled closed-panel slice.",
    "The additional visible-panel difference is diagnostic context only. Subtracting a same-session baseline cannot change the failed declared B/D ceiling verdict.",
    "Window selection is post-hoc. Native tab-change timestamps and deferred Unity rendering/destruction are uninstrumented. The data do not distinguish UDS background callbacks, injected-menu/native rendering cost and session differences."
  ],
  "Decision": "Prepare one opt-in timing interval separating panel-open/closed Update and synchronous UI paths. No ordinary runtime correction is justified from these slices alone. No further unchanged baseline series is requested."
